        "description": "<p>To comply with Australia&#39;s <a data-i13n=\"cpos:1;pos:1\" href=\"https://www.engadget.com/social-media/australia-is-adding-twitch-to-its-social-media-ban-for-children-202033276.html\">under-16 social media ban</a>, Meta said on <a data-i13n=\"cpos:2;pos:1\" href=\"https://medium.com/meta-australia-policy-blog/update-on-metas-compliance-with-social-media-age-ban-law-7d811845db60\">Medium</a> that it has shut down nearly 550,00 accounts. That number includes 330,000 Instagram, 173,000 Facebook and 40,000 Threads accounts deemed to belong to children. &quot;Ongoing compliance with the law will be a multi-layered process that we will continue to refine, though our concerns about determining age online without an industry standard remain,&quot; the company wrote.&nbsp;</p>\n<p>Australia&#39;s minimum age social media ban, the first of its kind in the world for a democracy, <a data-i13n=\"cpos:3;pos:1\" href=\"https://www.esafety.gov.au/about-us/industry-regulation/social-media-age-restrictions/f",
